{"id": "sc-017", "question": "I got 96% in my Plus 2 board exams. What tuition fee waiver can I get?", "category": "scenario", "split": "tuning", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/2-plus_2_board_examination_performance", "srm/scholarship/2-plus_2_board_examination_performance-2"], "required_values": ["15"], "forbidden_values": ["10% Tuition", "100%"], "note": "95 percentage and above in the Plus 2 board exam gives Merit Scholarship 15%: a 15% tuition fee waiver. 90-94.99 gives 10%."}
{"id": "sc-018", "question": "My father is a retired army officer. Can I get a scholarship, and what CGPA do I need to keep it?", "category": "scenario", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/12-defence_scholarship"], "required_values": ["8"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "Yes: the Defence Scholarship is for students whose parent is defence personnel in service, retired or deceased. Renewal needs a CGPA > 8, no arrears, and applying every year."}
{"id": "sc-019", "question": "I got rank 300 in SRMJEEE. Which scholarship can I get, and what CGPA must I keep to renew it?", "category": "scenario", "split": "tuning", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/scholarship/2-srm_merit_scholarship"], "required_values": ["9"], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "SRMJEEE ranks 101-500 qualify for the SRM Merit Scholarship; renewal is subject to maintaining a CGPA > 9, no arrears, and applying every year."}
{"id": "sc-020", "question": "The disciplinary committee punished me and I think the decision is wrong. How can I appeal?", "category": "scenario", "split": "heldout", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/code_of_conduct/7-appeal_process"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "Appeal in writing to the Registrar, who may refer it back to the disciplinary committee or convene the Appellate Committee headed by the Vice-Chancellor, whose decision is final. Appeals are permitted only for Level 5 and Level 6 misconduct."}
{"id": "sc-021", "question": "I rewrote the ideas from a published paper in my own words and did not cite it. Is that plagiarism?", "category": "scenario", "split": "tuning", "answerable": true, "expected_citations": ["srm/academic_integrity/4-paraphrasing_plagiarism_intellectual_the"], "required_values": [], "forbidden_values": [], "note": "Yes. Paraphrasing - taking another person's writing and changing the words so it appears as one's own - is plagiarism (intellectual theft)."}
